{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q27293702","formula":"C₁₅H₁₁NO₃","hill":"C15H11NO3","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":15.0,"H":11.0,"N":1.0,"O":3.0},"names":{"en":"Cridanimod","ru":"Акридонуксусная кислота"},"descriptions":{"en":"Cridanimod, also known as cycloferon or meglumine acridone acetate, is a low molecular weight immunomodulatory drug known to trigger the production of interferons, which are proteins that play a crucial role in the immune response against viral infections. It is primarily used in the treatment and prevention of various viral infections, including influenza and acute respiratory viral infections (ARVI), as well as in managing conditions such as HIV and herpes infections.","ru":"Акридонуксусная кислота (10-карбоксиметил-9-акридон) — органическое соединение, низкомолекулярный индуктор интерферона, оказывает противовирусное, иммуностимулирующее, противовоспалительное действия. Основной активный компонент для изготовления лекарственных препаратов «Циклоферон», «Неовир», «Камедон». Брутто-формула: C15H11NO3."},"fame":4,"pubchemCid":38072,"mass":253.25,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1=CC=C2C(=C1)C(=O)C3=CC=CC=C3N2CC(=O)O","inchikey":"UOMKBIIXHQIERR-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"2-(9-oxoacridin-10-yl)acetic acid","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"38072","atoms":30,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-0.119,"y":-3.285,"z":0.113,"el":"O"},{"x":0.231,"y":4.321,"z":-0.054,"el":"O"},{"x":0.092,"y":2.606,"z":1.431,"el":"O"},{"x":0.018,"y":0.716,"z":-0.488,"el":"N"},{"x":-1.244,"y":0.119,"z":-0.262,"el":"C"},{"x":1.235,"y":0.034,"z":-0.262,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.322,"y":-1.266,"z":-0.02,"el":"C"},{"x":1.219,"y":-1.353,"z":-0.021,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.077,"y":-2.065,"z":0.024,"el":"C"},{"x":0.065,"y":2.113,"z":-0.928,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.454,"y":0.836,"z":-0.245